GAFUCHI CHEMICAL IND</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAGAWA YOSHIKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJITA, MASAYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANEKA CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAGAWA, YOSHIKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJITA MASAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAGAWA YOSHIKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJITA, MASAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAGAWA, YOSHIKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An acrylic rubber composition which has satisfactory handleability and gives a cross-linked object having satisfactory material properties. The composition comprises: (A) an acrylic polymer having at least one active halogen represented by the general formula (1) at an end of the main chain -CH2-C(R&lt;1&gt;)(R&lt;2&gt;)(X) (1) (wherein R&lt;1&gt; and R&lt;2&gt; are the same or different and each represents a hydrogen atom or monovalent organic group derived from a group bonded to the vinyl group of a vinyl monomer as a component of the main chain; and X represents chlorine, bromine, or iodine) and (B) a cross-linking agent.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition de caoutchouc acrylique présentant une bonne maniabilité et permettant d'obtenir un article réticulé présentant de bonnes propriétés matérielles. Ladite composition comprend: (A) un polymère acrylique comportant au moins, à une extrémité de la chaîne principale, un halogène actif représenté par la formule générale (1) (dans laquelle R&lt;1&gt; et R&lt;2&gt;, identiques ou différents, représentent chacun un atome d'hydrogène ou un groupe organique monovalent dérivé d'un groupe lié au groupe vinyle d'un monomère vinylique entrant dans la composition de la chaîne principale -CH2-C(R&lt;1&gt;)(R&lt;2&gt;)(X); et X représente le chlore, le brome, ou l'iode), et (B) un agent de réticulation.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>